# Copy to `.env` only if you need to override the default.
#
# Leaving DATABASE_URL unset is fine for local development: the app falls back to
# a SQLite file at prisma/dev.db (see src/server/db/database-url.ts).
#
# SQLite (default):
# DATABASE_URL="file:./prisma/dev.db"
#
# Postgres (see docs/backend.md before switching):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://soko:soko@localhost:5432/soko?schema=public"

# --- Firebase (client) ---
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in from the Firebase console:
#   Project settings -> Your apps -> SDK setup and configuration.
#
# These are public identifiers, not secrets. A Firebase web API key is served to
# every visitor in the client bundle by design; Google documents it as safe to
# expose. What protects the project is Security Rules and App Check — never
# treat these as credentials, and never assume a locked-down repo is protection.
#
# All are required except MEASUREMENT_ID, without which Analytics is skipped.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=""
